## 6. Frontend components & pages

### Structure

- Component folder: `Name/Name.tsx` + `Name.module.scss`; children under `_components/Child/`.
- Default export: `export default function Name`.
- Props type: `NameProps` (or loaded/loading split like `OfferItem`).
- Landing sections: server component when possible; `'use client'` only for hooks/sockets/motion.
- App routes: thin **server** `page.tsx` (auth, metadata, shell) + **`page.client.tsx`** for interactive UI (tasks pattern).

### Landing patterns

- Compose the page from section components; pass `initialHomepagePromise` into client islands; wrap promise consumers in `<Suspense fallback={<NamedFallback />}>`.
- Section title block: eyebrow `h3` + `t.rich('title', { highlight: (chunks) => <span>{chunks}</span> })` + description `p`.
- Module-level `as const` key lists (`FAQ_IDS`, `EARN_METHODS`) instead of inline magic strings.
- Pure helpers and fallbacks as sibling `function` declarations in the same file.

### Tasks / offers UI patterns

- Filter option configs at module scope with **i18n label keys**, map to `t(...)` at render time (`SORT_OPTIONS`, `CATEGORY_OPTIONS`).
- URL/query state via dedicated params helpers (`tasksSearchParams` + `nuqs`); debounce/search: query against committed URL value when that is the established pattern.
- Infinite query in a hook (`useBrowseOffers`); page owns UI + intersection observer.
- Mark intentional floating promises: `void setFilters(...)`, `void fetchNextPage()`.
- Loading: skeleton `OfferItem loading`; empty state block; explicit load-more when capped.
- Default export wraps content in Suspense with a named fallback component.

### Class names

```tsx
className={[ styles.circle, styles.light ].join(' ')}
className={[ styles.root, cond ? styles.on : '', props.className ].filter(Boolean).join(' ')}
```

